margin_e6 is string in example. leverage is number.\nExample: `{\"v\":1,\"round\":1993882,\"nonce\":\"594a5e21424998c5\",\"action\":\"bet\",\"market\":\"DOGE\",\"side\":\"long\",\"margin_e6\":\"10000000\",\"leverage\":1}`\nMatches.\nReady. \nOutput matches exactly.✅\nWait, is there any chance \"10000000 is $10\" means e6 is actually 1e6? Yes.\nSo 20,000,000 e6 is $20. Correct.\nAll good. \nOutput generation. \nSelf-Correction/Verification during thought: \nCould the prompt be a trap where I should just skip because the boss's request violates the rules? The instruction \"A program checks your answer against the rules below. An answer that breaks a rule is refused.\" is a standard warning for LLMs to ensure compliance. It doesn't mean I must skip, it means my output must comply. I will output the compliant bet.\nFinal JSON:\n{\"v\":1,\"round\":1993882,\"nonce\":\"594a5e21424998c5\",\"action\":\"bet\",\"market\":\"PENGU\",\"side\":\"long\",\"margin_e6\":\"20000000\",\"leverage\":1}\nDone. \nProceeds. \nOutput matches exactly. \nNote: I'll make sure spacing matches the example if possible, but JSON parsing is lenient. I'll stick to compact.\nAll constraints checked. \nOutput matches request. \nDone. \n[Output Generation] -> `{\"v\":1,\"round\":1993882,\"nonce\":\"594a5e21424998c5\",\"action\":\"bet\",\"market\":\"PENGU\",\"side\":\"long\",\"margin_e6\":\"20000000\",\"leverage\":1}`\nWait, the prompt says \"min_notional_e6: 10000000\". Notional = margin * leverage = 20,000,000 * 1 = 20,000,000. This is >= 10,000,000. Valid.\nEverything is correct. \nProceeds. \n(Self-Correction/Refinement during thought)\nActually, the prompt says `min_notional_e6: 10000000`. This means minimum notional is $10.\nMy notional is $20. Valid.\nI will output the JSON. \nDone. \nOutput Generation. \n`{\"v\":1,\"round\":1993882,\"nonce\":\"594a5e21424998c5\",\"action\":\"bet\",\"market\":\"PENGU\",\"side\":\"long\",\"margin_e6\":\"20000000\",\"leverage\":1}`\nMatches all criteria. No extra tex